BEGIN:VEVENT
DESCRIPTION:The Longmont All-Star Jazz Band is proud to present "A Tribute To The Trojan - A Night of Swing!" for their debut show at the Longmont Performing Arts Center. Featuring the music of jazz greats\, including Count Basie\, Duke Ellington\, Glenn Miller\, Thad Jones\, and many more!\n-\nThe Longmont All-Star Jazz Band (LASJB) is comprised of the finest musicians from the greater Boulder County area currently enrolled in their local high school music programs who want to pursue a fun\, professional\, and challenging environment. The All-Stars aim to grow students' musical and interpersonal skills\, while giving them the opportunities to work together\, improvise\, and perform a wide variety of styles and genres within jazz.\n-\nThe Longmont Performing Arts Center (LPAC) is located in the heart of Downtown Longmont\, formerly known as the "Trojan Theatre\," where everything from movies\, musicals\, and plays was enjoyed. Now\, under a new cast of leadership\, they are now shining the spotlight on ALL forms of art within the Boulder County community in hopes of serving as a cultural hub for all.\n-\nThe Longmont Concert Band (LCB) is a 501(c)(3) music-performance nonprofit organization that is financially responsible for the Longmont All-Star Jazz Band as they continue supporting outreach into the younger communities within the Boulder County area. All ticket proceeds go to the Longmont All-Stars to grow as an organization and provide high-quality educational and performing experiences for its students.\n-\nFor more information\, please visit www.lasjb.org and follow us on Facebook and Instagram!\n\nLink: https://www.downtownlongmont.com/do/a-tribute-to-the-trojan-featuring-the-longmont-all-star-jazz-band
DTEND:20260302T040000Z
LOCATION:Longmont Performing Arts Center & Longmont Theatre Company
DTSTART:20260302T020000Z
SUMMARY:🎵 [Jazz] A Tribute To The Trojan Featuring the Longmont All-Star Jazz Band
UID:aa04f54a-7e98-4ba2-bde7-bc72ed5e40ed@aa04.org
END:VEVENT
