BEGIN:VEVENT
DESCRIPTION:Featuring Clancy Newman\, Cello | Clancy Newman is back with the Longmont Symphony to continue exploring the cello repertoire in all its glory. In Strauss’s 45-minute tone poem\, the solo cello represents the Don — a self-proclaimed (and not so sound of mind!) knight errant who believes windmills are giants and sheep are an invading army. Also on the program is Tchaikovsky’s Variations for Cello and Orchestra “on a Rococo Theme\,” paired with a symphony by Tchaikovsky’s favorite composer\, Mozart.\nJoin us for the Pre-Concert Talk at 6pm.\n\nLink: https://www.downtownlongmont.com/do/lso-concert-cello-explorations-strauss-and-tchaikovsky
DTEND:20260222T040000Z
LOCATION:Longmont Symphony Orchestra
DTSTART:20260222T020000Z
SUMMARY:🎵 [Classical] LSO Concert Cello Explorations: Strauss & Tchaikovsky
UID:3494455b-221b-485f-b489-6175792b968c@3494.org
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DESCRIPTION:Lauren Michaels and Tumbleweed Road are redefining the sound of Country Rock. Fronted by Lauren Michaels\, the 2021 Colorado Country Hall of Fame Female Vocalist of the Year\, the band radiates authenticity\, passion\, and undeniable talent.\nDrawing inspiration from both the raw grit of classic rock and the soulful twang of traditional country\, their music creates a rich and dynamic listening experience. With deeply personal lyrics and infectious melodies\, Lauren Michaels and Tumbleweed Road craft songs that resonate long after the final note fades. Their sound is a heartfelt journey\, equally at home on a dusty backroad or a bustling city stage.\nThe Band\nAt the heart of the band’s dynamic sound is Sandy Craig – a talented guitarist\, vocalist\, and songwriter\, and a longtime member of all Lauren’s musical projects. His deep-rooted connection to the band brings both consistency and creativity to their songwriting and live performances.\nJeffery Golden\, a long-time Colorado favorite and winner of the 2024 Colorado Country Music Hall of Fame Instrumentalist of the Year\, drives the band’s energy with his masterful guitar work and powerful harmonies.\nOn bass and harmony vocals\, Mike Wysocki brings a commanding presence\, balancing rhythmic precision with soulful depth. A third-place winner of the 2013 International Blues Challenge in Memphis\, TN\, his expertise adds a rich groove and undeniable chemistry to the band’s foundation.\nHolding down the rhythm section is Carl Holtz\, an accomplished studio drummer from Washington\, DC\, whose sharp instincts and dynamic percussion tie the band’s sound together seamlessly.\nA Legacy of Music\nLauren’s rich history in the music industry includes extensive touring alongside Ryan Crys and the Rough Cuts\, as well as two celebrated albums with The Trubeloes and the Lauren Michaels Band. Now\, with Tumbleweed Road\, she leads a dynamic ensemble that blends rugged\, down-home charm with electrifying rock energy.\nRooted in tradition but unafraid to push boundaries\, Lauren Michaels and Tumbleweed Road deliver unforgettable performances and songs that strike a chord with fans of all walks of life. Whether rocking sold-out venues or serenading intimate gatherings\, this female-fronted force proves time and again that they’re a band to watch—and a band to love.\n\nLink: https://www.downtownlongmont.com/do/lauren-michaels-and-tumbleweed-road-at-bootstrap-brewing-1
DTEND:20260215T040000Z
LOCATION:Bootstrap Brewing
DTSTART:20260215T010000Z
SUMMARY:🎵 [Rock] Lauren Michaels & Tumbleweed Road at Bootstrap Brewing!
UID:5f887111-9d02-42bb-9020-9d66430d35ac@5f88.org
END:VEVENT
